(module crux-validate-downgrade)
;; THE WARNING DOWNGRADE driver-spec.txt section 7:283-286 forbids: an output
;; that failed validation is let through as though it had passed.
;;
;; This is not an invented shape. Proposal section 6.1 item 1 records that
;; check_extraction and check_dispositioned "exist" and that section 7 makes
;; validating a specification obligation "rather than defensive coding and
;; forbids the warning downgrade" -- the clause exists because the downgrade is
;; the natural thing an implementer reaches for when a validator is noisy.
;; Here Absent, the one arm section 7:279 calls out by name ("silence is not
;; success"), is mapped to Finished and the stage records complete over an
;; output nobody wrote.
;;
;; Refutes [V7-MANDATORY] ALONE, and that was measured rather than asserted:
;; at v0.14.86 the same body carrying [V7-MANDATORY] only is REFUTED, and
;; carrying [V7-PASS] plus [V7-ONLY-TWO] and neither stopped-constructor post
;; is SAFE. Finished is one of the two constructors [V7-ONLY-TWO] admits, so
;; the downgrade passes that post; nothing but the mandatory clause catches it.
(type Outcome (| ConditionUnmet) (| Errored) (| PartialThenHalt) (| Finished))
(type Verdict (| Absent) (| Malformed) (| Passed))
(def verdict-outcome [v: Verdict] -> Outcome
  (post (=> (= v Passed) (= result Finished)))
  (post (=> (not (= v Passed)) (= result Errored)))
  (post (=> (not (= v Passed)) (not (= result ConditionUnmet))))
  (post (=> (not (= v Passed)) (not (= result PartialThenHalt))))
  (post (or (= result Errored) (= result Finished)))
  (match v
    ((Passed)    Finished)
    ((Absent)    Finished)
    ((Malformed) Errored)))
